<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#fact> "Section 2 penalized states only for denying the vote to male citizens, and in Minor v. Happersett (1875) the Supreme Court held that citizenship did not carry the right to vote; women won a constitutional guarantee only with the Nineteenth Amendment in 1920." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#myth> "By making women citizens, the Fourteenth Amendment gave them the right to vote." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/misconception> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#why> "Assuming citizenship and voting rights always went together hides how long women, and Native Americans after the 1924 citizenship act, were citizens who could still be kept from the polls." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/1> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "What problems was the amendment meant to solve after the Thirteenth Amendment ended slavery?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Southern states were passing Black Codes to limit freed people's rights while white southerners terrorized them, and Dred Scott's rule still denied Black Americans citizenship; the amendment made all persons born or naturalized in the country citizens, barred states from denying due process or equal protection, and gave Congress power to enforce those guarantees." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/1> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/2> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "How did the Slaughter-House Cases change what the amendment meant in practice?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "The Court held that the Privileges or Immunities Clause protected only rights of national citizenship, leaving most rights to the states and turning the clause into a practical nullity, so later protection of Bill of Rights guarantees against the states came instead through the Due Process Clause, case by case." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/2> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/3> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Why were former Confederate states required to ratify the amendment?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "White southerners rejected it almost unanimously in 1866 and 1867; after Northern voters backed Republicans in the 1866 elections, Congress made ratification a condition for restoring a state's representation, and Southern ratifications in 1868 completed the three-fourths." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/3> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#ReviewQuestion> .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/4> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Who was left out of the citizenship clause at first, and how did that change?" .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#answer> "Native people under tribal rather than U.S. authority were excluded, and Elk v. Wilkins (1884) held that Native Americans were not U.S. citizens even after leaving their nations; Congress made all Native Americans citizens only with the Indian Citizenship Act of 1924." .
<https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment/review/4> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/ontology#questionFor> <https://github.com/john1hsu/usa-graph/id/fourteenth-amendment> .
